From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: sdiohal_ctl: only declare pub_gpio_desc when parsing DT

The only uwe5622 warning left in a 7.3.1 build:

  drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c:758:27:
  warning: unused variable 'pub_gpio_desc' [-Wunused-variable]

pub_gpio_desc (>= 7.1) is only used inside the CONFIG_WCN_PARSE_DTS block,
which the Allwinner build does not define; pub_gpio_num (< 7.1) is used
unconditionally. Move the declaration under the same guard as its use.
No functional change.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c
index 0e03415..0b2e95b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_ctl.c
@@ -753,10 +753,11 @@ static int sdiohal_test_int_init(unsigned char func_tag)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_WCN_PARSE_DTS
 	struct device_node *np;
-#endif
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 1, 0)
 	struct gpio_desc *pub_gpio_desc = NULL;
-#else
+#endif
+#endif
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(7, 1, 0)
 	unsigned int pub_gpio_num = 0;
 #endif
 	unsigned char reg_int_en = 0;
-- 
Armbian
